WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.670
When rereading the Harry Potter books or watching
the movies, it's hard not to stumble onto

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.520
little inconsistencies here and there.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:11.240
From limited career options to the logistics
of Polyjuice Potion, these are just a few

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.420
Harry Potter details that don't make sense.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.460
After a young witch or wizard graduates from
Hogwarts, they're expected to join the adult

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.160
wizarding world, and part of that is figuring
out which career works for them.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.880
During the fifth book in the series, Order
of the Phoenix, Harry visits Professor McGonagall

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.830
for a required career advice meeting, and
they discuss which classes Harry should take

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.559
to qualify for his desired post-grad job.

00:00:33.559 --> 00:00:38.100
However, besides becoming an Auror — a "dark
wizard catcher" — post-Hogwarts options

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.850
seem pretty scarce, especially according to
the adults in Harry's life.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.770
It's never revealed what Harry's parents,
James and Lily, did for a living, but almost

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:49.620
every adult he knows growing up either works
for the wizarding government, the Ministry

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.789
of Magic, or teaches at Hogwarts.

00:00:51.789 --> 00:00:55.559
Though there is a wizarding hospital, St.
Mungo's, which is stocked with Healers, and

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:59.649
some talented athletes might become Quidditch
players, this means there are roughly four

00:00:59.649 --> 00:01:01.920
viable career paths in the wizarding world.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:06.000
The stage play Harry Potter and the Cursed
Child, which serves as a sort of sequel to

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.870
the original series, seems to confirm the
lack of career options — as adults, Harry,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:15.830
Ron and Hermione are all employed by the Ministry,
with Hermione even serving a term as the Minister

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:16.460
of Magic.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.880
In Harry's third year at Hogwarts, he discovers
the Marauder's Map, an enchanted, moving map

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:27.290
of Hogwarts that details every secret passageway,
contains every room, and shows the user where

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:30.900
every single person within the castle is and
whether or not they're on the move.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.520
A password-protected cheat sheet to the school,
the map is immensely useful to Harry throughout

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.711
his time at Hogwarts and beyond.

00:01:37.711 --> 00:01:42.250
And, as it turns out, it was his birthright
all along; Harry's father, James, helped create

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:43.960
the map during his own time there.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.000
“I solemnly swear that I am up to no good."

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.900
Harry is given the map by Ron's brothers Fred
and George, the notoriously mischievous Weasley

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:59.200
twins, who have been its custodians for years,
but this seems a bit off, considering that

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.090
the map apparently contained a huge, conspicuous
secret the entire time they had it.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:07.159
Peter Pettigrew, one of the map's creators
and the man who betrayed Harry's parents,

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:12.090
spent 12 years posing as Ron's pet rat and
sharing a dorm room with Ron and Harry, and

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:16.090
apparently, Fred and George didn't pay much
attention to the strange name hanging out

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:17.240
with their brother for years.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.080
The twins may be troublemakers, but they're
not stupid!

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.380
It just doesn't add up.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:26.280
One notable feature of Hogwarts is that it's
filled with magical, moving portraits, and

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.640
students and professors alike can communicate
with the seemingly sentient subjects within.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:34.780
From the portrait of the Fat Lady, who guards
the Gryffindor Common Room, to the former

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:39.000
headmasters and headmistresses living in their
own commemorative portraits in Dumbledore's

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.480
office, this world is filled with painted
personalities who are fully capable of carrying

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.140
on conversations with anyone who tries to
talk to them.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.300
“Password?"

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.840
"Caput Draconis."

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:54.680
"Wow."

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:58.660
Though Harry never directly learns the rules
of portraits, it seems as if they're only

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:03.520
created when a wizard dies; after Dumbledore's
death in Half-Blood Prince, his portrait appears

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:08.030
alongside his predecessors in the headmaster's
office, and as it turns out, he dispenses

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:11.640
advice to Severus Snape, who takes up the
post in the seventh book.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:16.700
Even so, the exact mechanics of these magical
portraits remain bafflingly unclear.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:20.560
There's definitely some part of the person
within the portraits, but does it only contain

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.320
the knowledge they possessed until their death,
or can the portraits continue to evolve?

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:29.040
"Eyes like the devil, he's got, and a soul
as dark as his name.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:30.860
It's him, headmaster.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.360
The one they all talk about.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:33.360
He's here.”

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:38.420
Every portrait Harry encounters seems to be
able to process and learn new information,

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:43.200
making the concept all the more confusing;
naturally, the magic behind this went unexplained

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.200
throughout the series.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.980
Harry encounters plenty of action and adventure
during his time in Hogwarts, which seems par

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.940
for the course for a kid constantly evading
the most dangerous dark wizard of all time.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:58.200
As a result, he also encounters plenty of
injuries — from regrowing all of the bones

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.540
in his arm to recovering from deadly curses.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.000
The medical staff at Hogwarts is usually on
high alert, and the school nurse, Madam Pomfrey

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.020
is capable of mending broken bones in the
blink of an eye.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.780
Madam Pomfrey's skills extend beyond life
and death circumstances as well; when Hermione

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:16.590
ends up cursed with expanding teeth, the nurse
shrinks them so that they're cosmetically

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:20.739
perfect, even though Hermione's teeth weren't
perfect before she was hit with the curse.

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:24.910
With that being said, it's a little odd that
so many characters in Harry's world, including

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.560
Harry himself, wear glasses.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:31.880
If Madam Pomfrey or any healer at St. Mungo's
can cure poisoned snake bites and broken legs,

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.460
why can't they fix something as simple as
astigmatism?

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:39.471
One of the most interesting potions in the
wizarding world is Polyjuice Potion, a brew

00:04:39.471 --> 00:04:43.480
that allows the user to transform into any
other person for one hour, as long as they

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:47.330
have a "bit" of that person — which, in
Harry's experience, typically means a hair

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.560
or two from the person's head.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:53.460
In Harry's second year, he and Ron impersonate
two Slytherin students, Crabbe and Goyle,

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:58.130
to figure out if Harry's nemesis, Draco Malfoy,
is using the Chamber of Secrets to attack

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.340
Muggleborn students.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:00.780
“Why are you wearing glasses?"

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:02.860
"Uh… um… reading."

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:04.200
"Reading?

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:07.720
I didn't know you could read."

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:12.200
Then, in Harry's fourth year, it turns out
that one of his professors is not the actual

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:16.520
Auror Mad-Eye Moody, but a Death Eater pretending
to be Moody thanks to the potion.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:21.680
Despite the difficult brewing process, Polyjuice
Potion is a constant factor throughout Harry's

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:22.180
journey.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:26.140
If Polyjuice Potion seems too good to be true,
you’re right — there are any number of

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:30.669
problems the user could encounter while using
it, beyond Hermione accidentally using a cat

00:05:30.669 --> 00:05:33.700
hair in Chamber of Secrets and ending up in
the hospital wing.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:37.960
Even if you look exactly like the person you're
impersonating, anyone who knows them well

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.340
enough would likely notice if your mannerisms
are off.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:44.810
The entire situation could be blown wide open
when someone whose hair has been used for

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:49.900
Polyjuice suddenly doesn't remember conversations
or experiences they had with other people.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:52.800
Polyjuice might seem foolproof, but it's far
from it.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.640
"You're lying, Dolores.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:58.880
And one mustn't tell lies.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.400
Stupefy!"

